nally scheduled for  release this year but it got delayed to  2021  this new third person action adventure  game is developed by ember lab  the same people who made the amazing  majora's mask fan film terrible fate so  it's no surprise that the trailer and  footage shown so far for bridge of  spirits is just as  full of atmosphere you play as a young  spirit guide named kina who's looking  for answers about a forgotten village  and a strange curse  he'll build a team of adorable tiny  spirit companions called rot that are  scattered throughout the land  these creatures will help you gain  abilities alter your environment and so  much more you will have to make use of  the fast-paced combat to defeat trapped  and corrupted spirits to help them move  on as you try to restore this  once majestic world ghostwire tokyo is a  first-person action adventure game where  99  of tokyo's population has vanished and  it's up to you to fight the supernatural  forces that caused it  the combat has been described as karate  meets magic as you use a series of  intricate martial arts inspired hand  gestures to cast spectral abilities and  take down various paranormal threats  from what we've seen so far you'll be  able to wield fire water and electrical  magic attacks along with a boat when  revealed in 2019  it was made clear that ghostwire isn't  like the survival horror games that  tango gameworks is known for but will  definitely still have some eerie  elements in the world  the game's combat director sinichirohara  has previously worked on doom 2016 more  specifically  the push forward combat and the glory  kill system so that might give you an  idea of what to expect  all in all i think kyra said it best  when he said we want the player to feel  like a badass  spellcasting high-tech ninja exorcist  defeating countless spirits  return is a third-person sci-fi shooter  with a few rogue-like elements where you  play as a space pilot who gets stranded  on an alien planet to make matters worse  you're also stuck in a time loop the  trailer and a few screenshots captured  on the ps5 show a variety of alien  enemies in a dark and creepy planet it's  up to you to find a way to break the  cycle and survive  in the trailer the main character says  with every death the world changes which  may be a key factor in the gameplay  not much else has been shown since  returnal's debut in june but the flashy  weapons and abilities mixed with this  mysterious story definitely have me  interested  here's another time loop extravaganza  but on the complete  other side of the spectrum def loop is a  first-person action adventure game where  you play as colt  an assassin who washed up on the shore  of black reef and needs to defeat eight  targets  in 24 hours to break the time loop he's  stuck in  while it may sound easy you have to deal  with it all while being hunted by rival  assassin  juliana while cole is trying to break  the loop juliana wants to keep it intact  and you can even play as her  in death loop's multiplayer and  infiltrate the games of others but when  it comes to the main story the puzzle  lies within how  and when you kill your targets changing  the course of the loop to get your  targets in more  optimal scenarios and doing it all  within a single day  the combat footage we've seen shows a  variety of guns and mobility options  like sprinting and sliding but there are  also special abilities like a teleport  and  launching enemies with the flick of a  wrist giving me huge  dishonored vibes the gameplay tone and  story already have me picturing ways to  conquer black wreath  revealed at dc fandom in august gotham  nights is an open world action rpg  that is set in its own universe so not  the batman arkham canon and takes place  after the death of batman you can play  as batgirl  nightwing red hood and robin to fight  against a new underworld that has taken  over gotham city you can play the entire  story solo  or into player co-op and each character  will have their own progression paths to  level up  gameplay footage has already been shown  off which gives us a good in-depth look  at how missions can be approached  differently depending on your character  and your play style we even got a close  look at one of the villains you'll face  mr freeze each boss difficulty and fight  style will scale and change  based on your level so a fight at level  5 will be different than the same fight  at level 50.  gotham knights is starting to look like  a really meaty game and honestly  i can't wait to sink my teeth into it  this one is for all the fighting game  heads out there  guilty gears drive is the newest  installment in the guilty gear series  and  it's returning with its iconic intense  gameplay there are 12 confirmed  characters so far with returning  favorites like soul bad guy  faust and more on the roster a new  mechanic added in strive  is the wall hit stick state where  certain attacks that you land on your  opponent near a wall will cause them to  stick to and slide down the wall itself  in this state you have a chance to break  the wall and transition the stage  similar to other fighting games like  tekken this could lead to more damage or  other setups guilty gear strive also  introduces a brand new character named  nagoriyuki who is a vampire with a  number  of unique and powerful abilities that he  uses alongside  a huge sword the sixth main installment  to the far cry series arrives in  february 2021 and is set in the  fictional country  of yara your goal is to take down yara's  dictator anton castillo who might look  familiar to you if you're a fan of  breaking bad  this first person shooter lets you play  as a gorilla fighter trying to take down  casio and his regime  castillo's son diego is another main  character in far cry 6.  another important detail is that the  thanks for hire system  is back in the form of amigos for hire  and i am  100 prepared to protect chirizo at all  cost  his tiny wheelchair is filled with ammo  and scopes and other things that will  assist you in combat  cd projekt red has announced that the  witcher 3 wild hunt is making its way to  next gen  if you already own it on ps4 or xbox one  you'll even get a free upgrade  the next gen edition will include ray  tracing faster loading  times and other improvements for not  only the base game but also both  expansions  and all extra content gta 5  may be 7 years old but it's still making  its way to the new consoles  playstation users get some special perks  for gta online such as a million in-game  bucks for every month you play gta 5 on  ps4  until it's released on ps5 you'll even  get to play gta online for free with a  ps plus membership for three months when  it's released the new version of gta 5  will have a range of technical  improvements  visual upgrades and performance  enhancements to take full advantage of  the latest hardware  that's 11 of the biggest games headed to  your playstation 5  next year which one are you looking  forward to the most let us know in the  comments and if you want to stay up to  date on more ps5 news and content then  be sure to keep your eyes peeled to the  gamespot youtube channel  you
 

